From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Willmer <info@jwillmer.de>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 13:34:32 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 087/111] Closing the last tab keeps the window with a new
 empty tab

As Close all already does. The window's own close button still quits.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/src/main.rs b/src/main.rs
index b2acf3f..b0477d6 100644
--- a/src/main.rs
+++ b/src/main.rs
@@ -2950,8 +2950,9 @@ impl App {
                 self.tab_model.remove(entity);
                 self.update_watcher();
 
-                // If that was the last tab, exit the application
-                if self.tab_model.iter().next().is_none() {
+                // If that was the last tab, keep the window with one new empty tab (as Close all
+                // does); the window's own close button quits
+                if self.tab_model.iter().next().is_none() && self.open_tab(None).is_none() {
                     return self.update(Message::QuitForce);
                 }
 
